WEBVTT

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.130
I definitely wasn't.

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:10.940
You were.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.670
Why would I look smug?

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:16.200
I don't know, but you did.

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:17.710
Welcome back.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:21.200
How did the teachers respond 
to the idea of an after party?

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.650
Not too well.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.860
Because you looked so smug.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:26.960
No, I didn't!

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.960
I outlined the budget.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.470
Thanks.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.470
Shall I print it out?

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.520
It's late. You can do it tomorrow.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:37.490
Okay.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.800
You're not leaving yet?

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:45.770
No.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:49.230
I'm staying a little late to go over 
the vice president's <i>PSO2</i> report.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.800
You can leave. Good work today.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.240
Good work.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:58.140
Excuse me, then.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.370
Do you have plans for 
this Saturday, President?

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:04.720
Saturday?

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:07.020
I think at Tensei Academy...

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.220
We have a meeting about the 
school festival, right?

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:10.750
In that case, I could join you.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:14.010
That's all right. I'll have the 
vice president accompany me.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:16.560
I see.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:19.070
I think I'm free the week after, though.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:20.760
Okay.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.640
Actually, never mind!

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:24.910
Excuse me!

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.510
Konoe-san.

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:29.320
What?

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:30.430
Why don't we group up sometime?

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:31.940
No, thanks.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:37.100
You failed to form a party with her?

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.090
Konoe-san's so cold.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.710
<b>Quest   07   Disappearance</b>

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:13.500
Vice president this, vice president that.

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:16.000
He's just an errand boy.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.850
I was the one always by her side before.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:25.640
Why am I getting jealous?

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:44.990
Aw, jeez! This is so annoying!

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.680
This is the last one!

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:53.250
What?

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:24.780
What was that?

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:25.920
What?

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:27.530
What is this? Why isn't it going away?

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:39.990
I bet you offended Mika somehow.

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:42.550
Maybe it's because of that thing
at the overnight trip.

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:43.700
What thing?

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:47.300
Suzuki-san?

00:04:58.090 --> 00:04:59.240
It disappeared?

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:09.830
Itsuki, you ranked.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.500
I did? I had no idea.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.870
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:18.430
You're pretty famous among the ARKS 
right now, because of your rapid growth.

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:19.360
Itsuki,

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:21.960
everyone's here.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:22.800
Oh, crap.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.710
There's a school festival committee meeting.

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:25.800
Oh, right.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.240
All the club presidents were
told to attend, too.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.560
Mika's not here?

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:34.280
No.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:37.700
Come to think of it, I haven't 
seen Konoe-san today.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.610
I was wondering,
| since she wasn't at breakfast.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:42.600
Sorry!

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:43.730
We're late!

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:46.560
Let's get started.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.990
Regarding After Party

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:48.990
An after party?

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:50.200
Yes.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:53.700
I'd like to hold one after the 
second day of the school festival.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:56.870
But we've never done one before.

00:05:57.140 --> 00:05:59.750
We used to hold one every year.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:04.780
There hasn't been one for the last ten years
because the school was against it.

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:08.760
We'd like to bring it back for 
this year's school festival.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.650
If we're going to hold an after party,

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:14.770
we'll need the cooperation 
of all classes and clubs.

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:19.550
We asked the club presidents to come here
so we could gain your understanding.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.520
What about permission from the school?

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:24.470
If the students are unanimous 
in their opinion,

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:26.490
the school will accept our wishes.

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:28.700
<i>Accept, huh?</i>

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:32.530
With all due respect, 
Seiga Academy's motto is

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:35.790
"student independence and creativity."

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:38.900
<i>She overpowered the teachers with logic...</i>

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:43.790
All right. If all the students 
are for it, we'll consider it.

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:48.810
<i>That was definitely a smug look of triumph.</i>

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:51.640
I'm opposed.

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:57.810
We're already putting a lot of time and effort
into preparing for the school festival.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:01.060
I don't think there's any point in 
willingly increasing our workload.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:05.610
I think it's an interesting idea for the students
to organize an after party by themselves.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:08.460
Participation should be made voluntary, then.

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:14.720
I wasn't expecting so much opposition
to the after party.

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:19.530
And Izumi-senpai's been saying since she became
president that she wants to hold one, too.

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:21.190
It's too soon to give up.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:24.460
B-But if we're too forceful, won't we 
be met with even more opposition?

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:27.960
S-Sorry.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:33.570
True, bulldozing the opposition and making the
president look like a dictator isn't a good plan.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:37.140
Even without that, there've been
concerns raised about

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:42.230
President Izumi's repeated lobbying of the school
lately, be it over online games or anything else.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:46.250
Somebody has to speak up,
or nothing will ever change.

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:50.040
What? Mika's not at the dorm?

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:51.410
Yeah.

00:07:51.730 --> 00:07:55.490
I just overhead the teachers 
talking in the faculty office.

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:57.720
Her door was locked,

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:01.000
but when they had the guard open it,
there was no one inside.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.350
No way.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.720
Why the sudden interest in an after party?

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:17.700
It's not sudden. I've been 
thinking about it for a while.

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:21.370
I wanted us to do something ourselves,

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:23.590
instead of just the events 
chosen by the school.

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:26.040
Is that the only reason?

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:29.300
My third year of junior high...

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:30.230
What?

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:33.240
The students were going to
organize an after party,

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:37.240
but I opposed it because it would've
meant more work for us.

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:40.260
Just like the club presidents today.

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:41.750
But then...

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:47.750
The rest of the students, even those who'd never
got along, began planning something together.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:50.320
I felt like I'd been left behind.

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:52.760
I wished that I had done it after all.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:57.520
In that moment, I wondered 
what it would be like

00:08:57.990 --> 00:09:00.480
to work together towards a single goal.

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:05.020
<i>Student council members Izumi Rina-san
and Tachibana Itsuki-kun.</i>

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.020
<i>Please report to the faculty office.</i>

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:10.930
Konoe-san's missing?

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:12.890
She was absent without leave,

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:16.030
so we contacted the dorm
and had them check her room.

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:20.030
We can't get in touch 
with her parents, either.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:23.700
Do you have any idea where she is?

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:25.140
No.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:31.020
Don't you know Konoe-san's
phone number or e-mail address?

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:34.460
She's not answering her phone or messages.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:36.610
I'm not so sure.

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:39.880
It's not like I always grouped with Mika.

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:44.470
She seemed to have been playing in 
her dorm room or at cafés sometimes.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.040
Suzuki-san.

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:48.360
Thanks for the information.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:51.980
What did she ask about?

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:55.060
If Mika played <i>PSO2</i>.

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:56.420
<i>PSO2</i>?

00:09:56.680 --> 00:10:00.240
Apparently she was asking 
other classes the same thing.

00:10:04.030 --> 00:10:05.110
Welcome back.

00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:06.400
Thanks.

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:08.910
Um, is Mika...

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:10.250
Is Konoe-san back?

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:14.060
We still can't get in touch with her parents.

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:17.510
If she doesn't come back, 
we're going to report it to the police.

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:22.800
The school said not to 
make a big fuss about it.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:23.510
Got it?

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:27.300
I understand.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:35.520
Mika?

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:50.830
<b>[Rappy]</b> The iconic mascot character of PSO2. A mysterious super-dimensional creature that appears anywhere and everywhere ARKS visit. Most are yellow, but there are various seasonal color varieties. Because they resemble birds, they are sometimes made the subject of fried chicken jokes.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:55.380
<b>[Lillipa]</b> The indigenous race of the planet Lillipa. As a pacifistic race, when encountered in the field, they are always being overpowered by Darkers. Due to their cute appearance, they are popular among ARKS as a kind of mascot, and costumes resembling Lillipa exist in the game. Their cry makes a "li-li" sound.

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:01.390
Suzuki-san? What are you doing 
here without permission?

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:03.390
I could ask you the same thing.

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:06.890
Well, I... uh...

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:09.890
Hey! What are you—

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:11.140
Stop that!

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:14.920
Suzuki-san!

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:18.640
Stop!

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:24.370
Sake Steamed Monkfish Liver

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:24.370
<b>Too hard!!
Too hard for an amateur!! (;_;)</b>

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:26.620
Monkfish liver?

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:30.120
What's your favorite food?

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:33.630
Monkfish liver.

00:11:33.980 --> 00:11:34.800
What?

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:36.860
I see...

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:40.380
<b>Monkfish Liver Center</b>

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:44.390
Do you have plans for 
this Saturday, President?

00:11:57.020 --> 00:11:58.010
Senpai.

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:01.780
Suzuki-san was in Konoe-san's room?

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:03.420
What was she doing?

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:04.570
I don't know.

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:09.540
She was asking around at school to 
see if Konoe-san played <i>PSO2</i>, too.

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:11.840
What? I don't get it.

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:15.700
I always thought she was strange, but...

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:18.800
Izumi-senpai, are you okay?

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:21.770
You look pretty tired.

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:25.550
I may have gotten carried away.

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:29.880
The school approved of online games.

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:34.010
Lately I had even made some friends.

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:37.310
I wasn't really paying attention to Mika.

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:41.490
But, Rina-senpai, you're busy being 
the student council president.

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:43.200
And now you're busy with the school festival.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:48.280
There may have been something 
she wanted to tell me.
